1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,400
He bought a six-foot bologna log. His plan was even bigger.

2
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:06,800
Vance wanted to beat the price of ordinary store sandwiches.

3
00:00:06,800 --> 00:00:10,200
Buying that many packaged sandwiches would cost over twelve hundred dollars.

4
00:00:10,200 --> 00:00:13,600
His homemade version came to just three hundred thirty-two dollars.

5
00:00:13,600 --> 00:00:17,000
The enormous bologna looked more like a fence post than lunch.

6
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:20,400
Suddenly, Vance's quiet kitchen looked like a busy sandwich shop.

7
00:00:20,400 --> 00:00:23,800
Store sandwiches often come with barely any fresh vegetables inside.

8
00:00:23,800 --> 00:00:27,200
Vance wanted every bite to feel like a proper meal.

9
00:00:27,200 --> 00:00:30,600
But plain meat and bread weren't going to impress anybody.

10
00:00:30,600 --> 00:00:34,000
Then his giant pot appeared, and the challenge got serious.

11
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:37,400
Sweet onions slowly turned golden as the whole kitchen filled with aroma.

12
00:00:37,400 --> 00:00:40,800
Even Vance looked surprised by how delicious everything suddenly smelled.

13
00:00:40,800 --> 00:00:44,200
Next came a mountain of cheese that seemed impossible to finish.

14
00:00:44,200 --> 00:00:47,600
The deli slicer made his giant sandwich dream feel real.

15
00:00:47,600 --> 00:00:51,000
Then Vance revealed the ingredient nobody expected in this sandwich marathon.

16
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:54,400
An unbelievable number of eggs covered the wide metal griddle.

17
00:00:54,400 --> 00:00:57,800
He laid out twenty-eight bread slices at once for the crowd.

18
00:00:57,800 --> 00:01:01,200
That tiny kitchen toaster never stood a chance against this plan.

19
00:01:01,200 --> 00:01:04,600
With the bread perfectly toasted, the real mountain began rising.

20
00:01:04,600 --> 00:01:08,000
Soon the dining table disappeared beneath an enormous wall of sandwiches.

21
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:11,400
Hundreds of towering sandwiches stood in rows across the table.

22
00:01:11,400 --> 00:01:14,900
Each one held eggs, onions, cheese, and plenty of filling.

23
00:01:14,900 --> 00:01:18,300
But Vance wasn't making all this food for himself.

24
00:01:18,300 --> 00:01:21,800
After dark, yellow crates packed with sandwiches filled the station wagon.

25
00:01:21,800 --> 00:01:25,200
The real destination was a community room filled with children.

26
00:01:25,200 --> 00:01:28,600
One ordinary evening suddenly became a huge neighborhood dinner.

27
00:01:28,600 --> 00:01:32,000
The best part wasn't the massive pile of homemade sandwiches.

28
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:35,495
It was watching everyone smile when they finally shared them.

